 "text": "9/30/26, 5:12 AM\ne A field in which you specify the new premise.\n\nFeatures\nYou can use the following examples to identify which installation and point of delivery are identified and which data is reallocated.\n\nSe Example\n\nYou have two installations that are allocated to a premise. Both installations have the same point of delivery:\n\nInstallation\n\nA\n\nPremise                         Premise\nV_ALT                           V_ALT\n\n\u201c  a\n\nPoint of Delivery\nZP_XXX\n\nReallocate Point of Delivery/Installation to New Premise - Example 1\n\nIdentification\n\ne If you specify installation A and a new premise V_NEU in transaction ES64, the system identifies installation A,\ninstallation B and point of delivery ZP_XXX.\n\ne If you specify installation B and a new premise V_NEU in transaction ES64, the system also identifies installation A,\ninstallation B and point of delivery ZP_XXX.\n\ne If you specify point of delivery ZP_XXX and a new premise V_NEU in transaction ES64, the system also identifies\ninstallation A, installation B and point of delivery ZP_XXX.\n\nReallocation\n",
